This is not quite how I remember the upshot of the discussion. Here's
my understanding:

1. With "hunt" gismu (sisku, troci, nitcu, djica, etc.) as currently
defined, the x2 must be transparent.
2. To get an opaque reading, you need to have two syntactic layers
matching the two semantic layers (so you can stick quantifier in
subordinate bridi).
3. To get two syntactic layers matching the two semantic layers, you
need a different brivla.
4. It would be better to redefine all "hunt" gismu so that their syntax
matches their semantics, but that's not how things are at present, and
Lojbab has shown no signs of intending to revise them.

As for xe'V, it's never been formally proposed, so for the time being
we must do everything in forethought (which works, except for imperatives
and illocutionary-force-affecting cmavo in UI). (I was originally in
favour of ways of signalling scope in afterthought, but now I'm not,
because there is no sufficiently general solution.)
